# Vue template attributes

When an HTML/Vue tag has **more than one attribute**, put each attribute on its own line and put the closing `>` or `/>` on the next line.

**Wrong (multiple attributes on one line):**
```vue
<div class="login-redirection-view" data-testid="login-redirection-view">
<AuthCallback :clientId="clientId" />
```

**Correct (one attribute per line, closing on new line):**
```vue
<div
	class="login-redirection-view"
	data-testid="login-redirection-view"
>
<AuthCallback
	:clientId="clientId"
/>
```

- One attribute per line.
- Closing `>` or `/>` on its own line after the last attribute.
- Indent attributes and closing bracket with a tab (project uses tabs).
- Tags with only one attribute may stay on one line (ESLint allows it).
